---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import TaleList from '../../components/TaleList.astro';
import { cinemaNotes, pad } from '../../lib/site';
import '../../styles/hot-takes.css';
const entries = [...cinemaNotes].reverse();
---
<Base page="archive" title="Hot Takes" description="Films, documentaries and series, read closely: reviews, scene essays and craft notes from an independent critic's notebook." accent="#ec6f9b">
  <div class="cinema-nb">
    <section class="cn-hero wrap" aria-labelledby="cn-title">
      <div class="cn-hero-copy">
        <div class="eyebrow mono">Line 04 · Hot takes</div>
        <h1 id="cn-title" data-split>Films. Frames.<br /><em>Perspectives.</em></h1>
        <p class="cn-intro">Not a verdict and not a star rating. An informed account of an encounter with a work: what is on screen, what it might mean, and whether it works.</p>
        <span class="cn-kicker mono">Experience first. Interpretation second. Criticism third.</span>
      </div>
      <aside class="cn-slate" aria-label="First take status">
        <div class="cn-slate-top mono"><span>SCENE 01</span><span>TAKE 01</span></div>
        <div class="cn-slate-mark">CN</div><div class="cn-slate-rule"></div>
        <div class="cn-slate-label mono">THE FIRST TAKE</div><strong>Film to be locked</strong>
        <div class="cn-slate-foot mono"><span>STATUS</span><b>IN THE EDITING ROOM</b></div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="cn-layers wrap" aria-labelledby="cn-layers-title">
      <div class="cn-head"><span class="eyebrow mono">01 / How an argument is built</span><h2 id="cn-layers-title">Three layers.<br /><em>Never blurred.</em></h2></div>
      <div class="cn-grid">
        <article><span class="mono">A / Observation</span><h3>What is on screen</h3><p>The frame, the cut, the pause, the sound. Only what can actually be seen and heard.</p></article>
        <article><span class="mono">B / Interpretation</span><h3>What it might mean</h3><p>The reading that the choices support, with other plausible readings left open.</p></article>
        <article><span class="mono">C / Evaluation</span><h3>Whether it works</h3><p>A judgement that explains itself, so a reader who disagrees still sees the route.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cn-current wrap" aria-labelledby="cn-current-title">
      <div class="cn-current-head"><div><span class="eyebrow mono">02 / Current reel</span><h2 id="cn-current-title">The first take is <em>still being framed.</em></h2></div><span class="mono cn-index">{pad(entries.length)} {entries.length === 1 ? 'take' : 'takes'} published</span></div>
      {entries.length > 0 ? <TaleList items={entries} /> : <div class="cn-empty">
        <div class="cn-empty-stamp mono">RESERVED · 001</div>
        <div><h3>No film has been locked yet.</h3><p>The opening piece is a director's-craft study: how a screenplay was written, how it was envisioned, and how the actors carried out the plan as the director's instrument. Structure and draft to follow.</p></div>
        <div class="cn-empty-status mono"><span>STRUCTURE</span><b>PENDING</b><span>DRAFT</span><b>PENDING</b></div>
      </div>}
    </section>

    <section class="cn-closing wrap"><p>Independent criticism. Spoiler warnings where they are earned, facts checked, and any access or sponsorship disclosed.</p><a class="mono" href="#cn-layers-title" data-cursor="link">Back to the top ↑</a></section>
  </div>
</Base>
